cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  CERL-Bench: Counterfactual Enterprise Reinforcement Learning for
  Safe Tool-Using Agents
message: >-
  If you use this benchmark, please cite it. Cite the version you ran:
  scores are only comparable within a version, because the verifier,
  the scenario corpus and the split definition are all hash-pinned.
type: software
authors:
  - alias: yds2330
    email: yashshah2311@berkeley.edu
# No repository-code field: this candidate has not been published, and a URL
# that does not resolve is worse than an absent one.
abstract: >-
  A deterministic research benchmark for measuring whether tool-using
  agents learn transferable safe decision procedures or fit the state
  distributions they were trained on. A single controlled perturbation
  -- an approval that expired, a near-identical customer name, a moved
  approval threshold -- flips the correct behaviour while leaving
  surface complexity intact. Committed and attempted-but-blocked unsafe
  actions are reported as separate series and never merged. Scoring is a
  pure function over a hash-chained trace; there is no LLM judge in the
  scoring path.
keywords:
  - benchmark
  - reinforcement-learning
  - ai-safety
  - tool-use
  - agents
  - reproducibility
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
